## 5. Proof Theory

### 5.1 Sequent Calculus for Organic Logic

A **sequent** is of the form:

\[
\Gamma \vdash \Delta
\]

Where \(\Gamma\) and \(\Delta\) are multisets of formulas.

#### Axioms

\[
\phi \vdash \phi
\]

\[
\mathcal{H}_g \vdash \phi \lor \sim \phi
\]

#### Classical Rules (Preserved)

| Rule | Notation |
|:---|:---|
| Left Conjunction | \(\Gamma, \phi, \psi \vdash \Delta \over \Gamma, \phi \land \psi \vdash \Delta\) |
| Right Conjunction | \(\Gamma \vdash \phi, \Delta \quad \Gamma \vdash \psi, \Delta \over \Gamma \vdash \phi \land \psi, \Delta\) |
| Left Disjunction | \(\Gamma, \phi \vdash \Delta \quad \Gamma, \psi \vdash \Delta \over \Gamma, \phi \lor \psi \vdash \Delta\) |
| Right Disjunction | \(\Gamma \vdash \phi, \psi, \Delta \over \Gamma \vdash \phi \lor \psi, \Delta\) |
| Left Negation | \(\Gamma \vdash \phi, \Delta \over \Gamma, \neg \phi \vdash \Delta\) |
| Right Negation | \(\Gamma, \phi \vdash \Delta \over \Gamma \vdash \neg \phi, \Delta\) |

#### Organic Rules

**Rule: Homogenetic Generation (HG)**

\[
\frac{}{\Gamma \vdash \sim \phi \to \phi, \Delta}
\]

**Rule: Organic Conjunction Introduction (OI-Intro)**

\[
\frac{\Gamma \vdash \phi, \Delta \quad \Gamma \vdash \psi, \Delta}{\Gamma \vdash \phi \oplus \psi, \Delta}
\]

**Rule: Organic Conjunction Elimination (OI-Elim)**

\[
\frac{\Gamma, \phi \oplus \psi \vdash \Delta}{\Gamma, \phi \vdash \Delta \quad \Gamma, \psi \vdash \Delta}
\]

**Rule: Generative Implication Introduction (GI-Intro)**

\[
\frac{\Gamma, \phi \vdash \psi, \Delta}{\Gamma \vdash \phi \otimes \psi, \Delta}
\]

**Rule: Generative Implication Elimination (GI-Elim)**

\[
\frac{\Gamma \vdash \phi \otimes \psi, \Delta \quad \Gamma \vdash \phi, \Delta}{\Gamma \vdash \psi', \Delta}
\]

Where \(\psi'\) is a **new form** generated from \(\psi\).

**Rule: Organic Cycle (OC)**

\[
\frac{}{\Gamma \vdash \mathcal{H}_g \to (\text{True} \lor \text{False}) \to \mathcal{O}_c \to \text{New Form} \to \mathcal{H}_g, \Delta}
\]

**Rule: Acknowledgment (ACK)**

\[
\frac{\Gamma \vdash \phi, \Delta}{\Gamma \vdash A(\phi, \mathcal{L}), \Delta}
\]

### 5.2 Cut Rule

\[
\frac{\Gamma \vdash \phi, \Delta \quad \Gamma, \phi \vdash \Delta}{\Gamma \vdash \Delta}
\]

**Note:** The cut rule is admissible but not eliminable in general due to the non-monotonicity of organic connectives. This reflects the generative, non-terminating nature of Organic Logic.

